==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|last|ly|lang=en}}.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|sequence}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to mark the beginning of the last in a list of items or propositions.}}
#: ''Firstly, that's illegal; secondly, it has serious disadvantages; thirdly, it's not necessary; and '''lastly''', did I mention that it's illegal?''
# {{lb|en|discourse marker}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to signal that the speaker is about to yield control of the conversation}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|last in order}} {{l|en|finally}}, {{l|en|last}}, {{l|en|last of all}}
* {{sense|discourse marker}} {{l|en|finally}}, {{l|en|to conclude}}, {{l|en|to sum up}}, {{l|en|in conclusion}};<!--The following may be too ambiguous to serve as valid discourse marker--> [[ultimately]], [[in the end]], [[all in all]], [[at last]]

